 "figures": {
  "map": {
   "title": "Healthy, and diverse?",
   "caption": "Each dot is a world at its last checkpoint. Across: how many of the seven marks of Chapter 46's health bar it meets \u2014 one piece, a 2-core of at least 0.8, no agent whose loss cuts off more than 2%, no link more than 1%, no agent joined to more than 5% of the others, 3 to 12 links per agent, a dimension of 2.3 to 4 (the dots are spread sideways within each count only so that they do not hide each other). Up: how widely its agents spread over tokens, links, ages and genotypes, as the mean of its percentiles among all worlds. The author's picture of a world that might keep evolving is the top right. B1: B1 at every size and its variants (Experiments 2, 8, 10, 12, 13); brains fixed: Experiment 7; B2: B2 and its variants (Experiments 9, 14, 15, 16), except lapse, where any unused link lapses; long runs: the pilot worlds played to 10,000 iterations; pilots: the other pilot worlds, by the rule set they start from.",
   "recipe": "**Runs.** Every world the book has made that settled (500 iterations or more), each once, at its last checkpoint: the lab's runs at their end, the pilot worlds at theirs, the long runs at 10,000 iterations; pilots that replay a lab world are counted as that world (`python3 research/atlas/profile.py`).\n\n**Data.** From `GraphOfLifeRuns/.pilots/atlas/profile.json`.\n\n1. Read each world's checkpoint: its agents' tokens, links, birth times and genotypes.\n2. The network: pieces, the 2-core, the worst cut by one agent and by one link (one depth-first search), the best-connected agent's share, links per agent; the dimension from the table of every world.\n3. The spreads: the effective number of doubling classes the agents fill (exp of the entropy), for tokens, links and ages; genotypes per agent (1 / sum of squared shares, over the agents).\n4. Rank every world on each spread; the score is the mean of its four percentiles.\n\n**To make it again:** `python3 book_figures.py healthy`."
  },
  "poor": {
   "title": "Agents with three tokens or fewer",
   "caption": "Each dot is a world: the share of its agents holding one, two or three tokens. B1 10k: B1 at 10,000 tokens (Experiment 2); 100k: Experiment 10; sizes: Experiment 8; 5k: Experiments 12 and 13; fixed: brains that never change (Experiment 7); B2 10k: Experiment 16; B2 var: B2 with one rule or rate changed (Experiments 9, 15, 16); B2 5k: Experiment 14, except lapse, where any unused link lapses; long runs: the pilot worlds played to 10,000 iterations; pil.: the other pilot worlds, by the rule set they start from.",
   "recipe": "**Runs.** Every world the book has made that settled (500 iterations or more), each once, at its last checkpoint: the lab's runs at their end, the pilot worlds at theirs, the long runs at 10,000 iterations; pilots that replay a lab world are counted as that world (`python3 research/atlas/profile.py`).\n\n**Data.** From `GraphOfLifeRuns/.pilots/atlas/profile.json`.\n\n1. Count the agents of each world's checkpoint holding at most three tokens.\n\n**To make it again:** `python3 book_figures.py healthy`."
  },
  "spreads": {
   "title": "How widely the agents spread",
   "caption": "Each dot is a world. Tokens, links, ages: the effective number of doubling classes its agents fill (1, 2\u20133, 4\u20137, \u2026; for ages, age + 1) \u2014 1 if every agent is in one class, k if they are spread evenly over k. Genotypes: the effective number of genotypes per agent (1 for every agent its own genotype, near 0 for one genotype everywhere).",
   "recipe": "**Runs.** Every world the book has made that settled (500 iterations or more), each once, at its last checkpoint: the lab's runs at their end, the pilot worlds at theirs, the long runs at 10,000 iterations; pilots that replay a lab world are counted as that world (`python3 research/atlas/profile.py`).\n\n**Data.** From `GraphOfLifeRuns/.pilots/atlas/profile.json`.\n\n1. For each world, exp of the Shannon entropy of its agents' shares over the doubling classes of each quantity; the effective genotypes, 1 / sum of squared shares, per agent.\n\n**To make it again:** `python3 book_figures.py healthy`."
  }
